														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4086737">
									

<p>This is a -1 for me. No hesitation.</p>
<p>The idea here seems like it could work but the execution is a bit of a mess.</p>
<p>I don't feel anything really coherent about the way this is presented. I come into this immediately knowing what to expect out of it and it goes exactly as I imagined it would. There's no natural raising of stakes.</p>
<p>Those stakes are almost as high as they can be from the outset (with the secretary of state thing) and there's no subversion of expectations. That ruins any sort of coherent narrative arc when the piece is clearly trying to present a story.</p>
<p>I also don't get a strong sense of the thematic tone you're aiming for. Is this serious? Is it silly? It tries to be both and as a result only hits on either tone weakly. The starkly contrasting themes actually just makes the lack of good clinical tone throughout more apparent. I can see bits that are more silly that just don't really use good clinical language alongside bits that are serious and actually mostly hit the mark.</p>
<p>On top of that, there's insertion of interview logs with the pasta that do not seem to help develop anything in your story and aren't really good enough to work in the piece on their own.</p>
<p>Not to mention that there's blackboxing in the Containment procedures and while I have a personal opinion about overuse of blackbox that I am willing to put to the side most of the time <em>that</em> is something I cannot abide.</p>
<p>Good luck with your article!</p>

