														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4086748">
									

<p>This is an amusing idea, but I ended up downvoting. The core of a noodle that must be handled very carefully to prevent chaos is good, but there is a lot of additional fluff that sends the tone all over the place (as Cimmerian already said) and also felt derivative of other articles - the infinite noodle dimension and the bad-English interview logs in particular. The whole White House setting felt bizarre (not in a good way) as there is no thematic connection between the White House and noodles, it comes across as a hamfisted way to make this as troublesome as possible without justification, and is really the sort of thing that would lead to a Broken Masquerade canon, which has a particular feel this isn't going for. The weird grammar issues are also present (mostly strange capitalisation choices).</p>
<p>On a lighter note, the noodle designations are questionable (couscous? really?), as are the non-noodle designations (I wouldn't really consider farfalle to be a noodle, but it has about the same level of noodle-related properties as spätzle)</p>

							</div>

								
					
